{"module":"borders","voice":"male","duration":260.2,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Fronteras: quién puede ser estadounidense","start":0.0,"end":3.12,"words":[[0.03,0.81],[1.08,1.39],[1.39,1.78],[1.78,2.01],[2.01,3.1]]},{"el":"intro","text":"La ley de inmigración siempre ha sido una forma de decidir quién cuenta como estadounidense.","start":3.92,"end":9.37,"words":[[3.92,4.06],[4.06,4.26],[4.26,4.39],[4.39,5.13],[5.13,5.6],[5.6,5.67],[5.67,5.94],[5.94,6.14],[6.14,6.47],[6.47,6.61],[6.61,7.08],[7.08,7.35],[7.35,7.75],[7.75,8.02],[8.02,9.03]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Durante la mayor parte de la historia de EE. UU., lo hizo abiertamente según la raza.","start":9.72,"end":15.04,"words":[[9.77,10.23],[10.23,10.36],[10.36,10.68],[10.68,11.01],[11.01,11.14],[11.14,11.27],[11.27,11.73],[11.73,11.86],[11.86,12.05],[12.38,12.58],[12.81,12.94],[12.94,13.13],[13.13,13.92],[13.92,14.24],[14.24,14.37],[14.37,14.7]]},{"el":"h0","text":"“Personas blancas libres”","start":15.39,"end":17.28,"words":[[15.39,16.07],[16.07,16.68],[16.68,17.19]]},{"el":"s0","text":"La primera Ley de Naturalización (1790) limitó la ciudadanía por naturalización a las “personas blancas libres”.","start":17.98,"end":25.85,"words":[[18.0,18.13],[18.13,18.59],[18.59,18.79],[18.79,18.92],[18.92,19.84],[19.84,21.22],[21.45,21.84],[21.84,21.97],[21.97,22.7],[22.7,22.89],[22.89,23.81],[23.81,23.88],[23.88,24.08],[24.08,24.6],[24.6,25.06],[25.06,25.52]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Después, los tribunales tuvieron que decidir quién era blanco.","start":26.2,"end":30.41,"words":[[26.25,26.8],[27.04,27.25],[27.25,27.94],[27.94,28.49],[28.49,28.63],[28.63,29.11],[29.11,29.39],[29.39,29.59],[29.59,30.08]]},{"el":"s0","text":"En Ozawa (1922), la Corte Suprema dictaminó que un inmigrante japonés no lo era; en Thind (1923), que un inmigrante sij de la India tampoco, aunque los antropólogos lo clasificaban como “caucásico”.","start":30.76,"end":46.16,"words":[[30.79,30.94],[30.94,31.29],[31.29,33.01],[33.26,33.4],[33.4,33.76],[33.76,34.26],[34.26,34.9],[34.9,35.05],[35.05,35.19],[35.19,35.9],[35.9,36.4],[36.4,36.55],[36.55,36.69],[36.69,36.98],[37.23,37.37],[37.37,37.65],[37.65,39.44],[39.69,39.83],[39.83,39.98],[39.98,40.69],[40.69,40.91],[40.91,41.05],[41.05,41.19],[41.19,41.55],[41.55,42.12],[42.37,42.73],[42.73,42.94],[42.94,43.8],[43.8,43.94],[43.94,44.8],[44.8,45.09],[45.09,45.8]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Las barreras raciales a la naturalización no se eliminaron del todo hasta 1952.","start":46.51,"end":53.21,"words":[[46.55,46.76],[46.76,47.26],[47.26,47.83],[47.83,47.9],[47.9,48.04],[48.04,49.04],[49.04,49.18],[49.18,49.32],[49.32,50.03],[50.03,50.25],[50.25,50.53],[50.53,50.82],[50.82,52.81]]},{"el":"h1","text":"La Exclusión China","start":54.11,"end":55.62,"words":[[54.11,54.27],[54.27,55.08],[55.08,55.48]]},{"el":"s1","text":"La Ley Page (1875) prohibió en la práctica la entrada de mujeres chinas, y la Ley de Exclusión China (1882) prohibió la de trabajadores chinos: fue la primera ley de EE. UU. en excluir a un grupo por su nacionalidad.","start":56.32,"end":73.16,"words":[[56.32,56.45],[56.45,56.66],[56.66,56.93],[56.93,58.77],[59.01,59.49],[59.49,59.63],[59.63,59.76],[59.76,60.31],[60.31,60.44],[60.44,60.92],[60.92,61.06],[61.06,61.54],[61.54,62.01],[62.25,62.32],[62.32,62.46],[62.46,62.66],[62.66,62.8],[62.8,63.48],[63.48,63.82],[63.82,65.53],[65.77,66.24],[66.24,66.38],[66.38,66.52],[66.52,67.33],[67.33,67.81],[68.05,68.26],[68.26,68.39],[68.39,68.87],[68.87,69.07],[69.07,69.21],[69.21,69.42],[69.76,69.96],[70.3,70.44],[70.44,70.98],[70.98,71.05],[71.05,71.19],[71.19,71.53],[71.53,71.73],[71.73,71.87],[71.87,72.76]]},{"el":"s1","text":"No se derogó hasta 1943.","start":73.51,"end":76.57,"words":[[73.51,73.64],[73.64,73.77],[73.77,74.15],[74.15,74.4],[74.4,76.17]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Los inmigrantes chinos eran detenidos e interrogados en la isla Ángel, en la bahía de San Francisco (1910–1940).","start":76.92,"end":86.34,"words":[[76.95,77.16],[77.16,77.94],[77.94,78.37],[78.37,78.65],[78.65,79.29],[79.29,79.36],[79.36,80.14],[80.14,80.28],[80.28,80.42],[80.42,80.71],[80.71,81.13],[81.38,81.52],[81.52,81.66],[81.66,82.02],[82.02,82.16],[82.16,82.37],[82.37,83.01],[83.01,85.99]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Cuotas por raza","start":87.24,"end":88.43,"words":[[87.26,87.77],[87.77,88.03],[88.03,88.37]]},{"el":"s2","text":"La Ley de Inmigración de 1924 fijó cuotas basadas en el origen nacional de la población de EE. UU. en 1890, para favorecer a los europeos del norte, y prohibió casi toda la inmigración desde Asia.","start":89.13,"end":104.66,"words":[[89.15,89.29],[89.29,89.5],[89.5,89.64],[89.64,90.41],[90.41,90.55],[90.55,92.36],[92.36,92.64],[92.64,93.06],[93.06,93.55],[93.55,93.69],[93.69,93.83],[93.83,94.25],[94.25,94.81],[94.81,94.95],[94.95,95.09],[95.09,95.72],[95.72,95.86],[95.86,96.07],[96.42,96.63],[96.98,97.12],[97.12,98.65],[98.9,99.18],[99.18,99.81],[99.81,99.88],[99.88,100.09],[100.09,100.64],[100.64,100.85],[100.85,101.27],[101.52,101.59],[101.59,102.08],[102.08,102.36],[102.36,102.64],[102.64,102.78],[102.78,103.54],[103.54,103.89],[103.89,104.24]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Los eugenistas testificaron a su favor.","start":105.01,"end":108.36,"words":[[105.01,105.24],[105.24,106.01],[106.01,106.93],[106.93,107.01],[107.01,107.16],[107.16,107.62]]},{"el":"s2","text":"El sistema de cuotas duró hasta la Ley de Inmigración y Nacionalidad de 1965.","start":108.71,"end":115.21,"words":[[108.73,108.87],[108.87,109.37],[109.37,109.51],[109.51,109.94],[109.94,110.22],[110.22,110.51],[110.51,110.65],[110.65,110.86],[110.86,111.01],[111.01,111.79],[111.79,111.86],[111.86,112.72],[112.72,112.86],[112.86,114.85]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Mexicoamericanos: la repatriación y la “Operación Wetback”","start":116.11,"end":120.69,"words":[[116.14,117.54],[117.83,117.99],[117.99,119.06],[119.06,119.15],[119.15,119.31],[119.31,120.05],[120.05,120.55]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Durante la Gran Depresión (1929–1936), autoridades federales, estatales y locales expulsaron a cientos de miles de mexicanos y mexicoamericanos; las estimaciones van de unas 400,000 a más de un millón de personas, y muchas eran ciudadanas de EE. UU., incluidos niños.","start":121.39,"end":144.59,"words":[[121.4,121.91],[121.91,122.06],[122.06,122.35],[122.35,123.01],[123.01,126.86],[127.12,127.92],[127.92,128.65],[128.9,129.56],[129.56,129.63],[129.63,130.14],[130.14,130.94],[130.94,131.01],[131.01,131.52],[131.52,131.67],[131.67,132.03],[132.03,132.18],[132.18,132.83],[132.83,132.91],[132.91,134.15],[134.4,134.62],[134.62,135.49],[135.49,135.71],[135.71,135.86],[135.86,136.15],[136.15,138.26],[138.26,138.33],[138.33,138.55],[138.55,138.7],[138.7,138.84],[138.84,139.28],[139.28,139.42],[139.42,140.08],[140.33,140.41],[140.41,140.84],[140.84,141.14],[141.14,141.86],[141.86,142.01],[142.01,142.23],[142.59,142.81],[143.06,143.72],[143.72,144.16]]},{"el":"s3","text":"California pidió perdón en 2005.","start":144.94,"end":147.73,"words":[[144.95,145.63],[145.63,145.98],[145.98,146.39],[146.39,146.52],[146.52,147.34]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial, el Programa Bracero reclutó trabajadores mexicanos; en 1954, la “Operación Wetback” llevó a cabo deportaciones masivas.","start":148.08,"end":160.1,"words":[[148.11,148.6],[148.6,148.74],[148.74,149.23],[149.23,149.51],[149.51,150.08],[150.32,150.46],[150.46,151.03],[151.03,151.52],[151.52,152.01],[152.01,152.86],[152.86,153.56],[153.81,153.95],[153.95,156.13],[156.38,156.52],[156.52,157.15],[157.15,157.58],[157.58,157.86],[157.86,157.93],[157.93,158.21],[158.21,159.12],[159.12,159.69]]},{"el":"s3","text":"El gobierno afirmó haber expulsado a más de un millón de personas ese año; los historiadores consideran que esa cifra está inflada.","start":160.45,"end":168.91,"words":[[160.45,160.6],[160.6,161.17],[161.17,161.61],[161.61,161.89],[161.89,162.61],[162.61,162.68],[162.68,162.9],[162.9,163.04],[163.04,163.19],[163.19,163.62],[163.62,163.76],[163.76,164.34],[164.34,164.56],[164.56,164.84],[165.09,165.31],[165.31,166.17],[166.17,166.89],[166.89,167.04],[167.04,167.25],[167.25,167.61],[167.61,167.9],[167.9,168.48]]},{"el":"h4","text":"El encarcelamiento de japoneses-estadounidenses","start":169.81,"end":173.1,"words":[[169.81,169.96],[169.96,171.07],[171.07,171.22],[171.22,173.01]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La Orden Ejecutiva 9066 (febrero de 1942) llevó a la expulsión forzada de unas 120,000 personas de ascendencia japonesa de la costa oeste, dos tercios de ellas ciudadanas de EE. UU., a campos cercados con alambre de púas.","start":173.8,"end":193.17,"words":[[173.82,173.97],[173.97,174.34],[174.34,175.01],[175.01,176.5],[176.5,177.01],[177.01,177.16],[177.16,179.09],[179.35,179.65],[179.65,179.72],[179.72,179.87],[179.87,180.61],[180.61,181.13],[181.13,181.28],[181.28,181.58],[181.58,183.66],[183.66,184.25],[184.25,184.4],[184.4,185.14],[185.14,185.73],[185.73,185.88],[185.88,186.03],[186.03,186.4],[186.4,186.85],[187.11,187.33],[187.33,187.85],[187.85,188.0],[188.0,188.37],[188.37,189.11],[189.11,189.26],[189.26,189.48],[189.85,190.07],[190.33,190.41],[190.41,190.85],[190.85,191.45],[191.45,191.67],[191.67,192.19],[192.19,192.34],[192.34,192.71]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La Corte Suprema lo avaló en Korematsu (1944).","start":193.52,"end":197.93,"words":[[193.55,193.68],[193.68,194.01],[194.01,194.47],[194.47,194.6],[194.6,194.93],[194.93,195.06],[195.06,195.65],[195.65,197.61]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La Ley de Libertades Civiles de 1988 pidió perdón y pagó $20,000 a cada sobreviviente que había sido encarcelado, y en 2018 la Corte dijo que Korematsu “fue gravemente erróneo desde el día en que se decidió”.","start":198.28,"end":215.5,"words":[[198.3,198.45],[198.45,198.67],[198.67,198.82],[198.82,199.57],[199.57,200.09],[200.09,200.24],[200.24,202.26],[202.26,202.63],[202.63,203.08],[203.08,203.15],[203.15,203.45],[203.45,205.46],[205.46,205.54],[205.54,205.84],[205.84,206.81],[206.81,206.96],[206.96,207.33],[207.33,207.63],[207.63,208.52],[208.79,208.86],[208.86,209.01],[209.01,210.2],[210.2,210.35],[210.35,210.73],[210.73,211.02],[211.02,211.17],[211.17,211.85],[211.85,212.07],[212.07,212.82],[212.82,213.26],[213.26,213.64],[213.64,213.79],[213.79,214.08],[214.08,214.23],[214.23,214.38],[214.38,214.53],[214.53,215.13]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Hoy","start":216.4,"end":217.12,"words":[[216.4,216.93]]},{"el":"s5","text":"En 2018, la política de “tolerancia cero” separó a miles de niños de sus padres en la frontera.","start":217.82,"end":224.83,"words":[[217.84,217.98],[217.98,219.22],[219.47,219.61],[219.61,220.19],[220.19,220.34],[220.34,221.06],[221.06,221.35],[221.35,221.79],[221.79,221.86],[221.86,222.22],[222.22,222.37],[222.37,222.73],[222.73,222.88],[222.88,223.09],[223.09,223.53],[223.53,223.67],[223.67,223.82],[223.82,224.47]]},{"el":"s5","text":"La detención migratoria retiene a decenas de miles de personas en un día cualquiera.","start":225.18,"end":230.81,"words":[[225.18,225.33],[225.33,226.0],[226.0,226.74],[226.74,227.26],[227.26,227.33],[227.33,227.85],[227.85,228.0],[228.0,228.37],[228.37,228.52],[228.52,229.11],[229.11,229.26],[229.26,229.41],[229.41,229.71],[229.71,230.45]]},{"el":"s5","text":"En septiembre de 2025, la Corte Suprema permitió que los agentes de inmigración en el área de Los Ángeles reanudaran las detenciones en la calle que un tribunal inferior había considerado basadas en factores como la etnia aparente, el idioma y el tipo de trabajo, mientras el caso continúa.","start":231.16,"end":251.53,"words":[[231.16,231.31],[231.31,232.07],[232.07,232.22],[232.22,233.59],[233.85,234.0],[234.0,234.38],[234.38,234.91],[234.91,235.52],[235.52,235.67],[235.67,235.9],[235.9,236.43],[236.43,236.58],[236.58,237.41],[237.41,237.56],[237.56,237.72],[237.72,238.02],[238.02,238.17],[238.17,238.4],[238.4,238.93],[238.93,239.69],[239.69,239.91],[239.91,240.75],[240.75,240.9],[240.9,241.05],[241.05,241.43],[241.43,241.58],[241.58,241.73],[241.73,242.34],[242.34,242.94],[242.94,243.32],[243.32,244.16],[244.16,244.69],[244.69,244.84],[244.84,245.44],[245.44,245.75],[245.75,245.9],[245.9,246.28],[246.28,246.96],[247.22,247.38],[247.38,247.83],[247.83,247.91],[247.91,248.06],[248.06,248.36],[248.36,248.51],[248.51,249.12],[249.38,249.99],[249.99,250.14],[250.14,250.44],[250.44,251.13]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Una ley tipo CAREN protege a cualquier persona, sea ciudadana o no, de ser denunciada a la policía para discriminarla.","start":251.88,"end":259.33,"words":[[251.94,252.14],[252.14,252.34],[252.34,252.6],[252.6,252.94],[252.94,253.4],[253.4,253.47],[253.47,254.0],[254.0,254.54],[254.77,254.97],[254.97,255.57],[255.57,255.64],[255.64,255.84],[256.07,256.2],[256.2,256.4],[256.4,257.07],[257.07,257.14],[257.14,257.27],[257.27,257.8],[257.8,258.07],[258.07,259.01]]}]}